@* AdminUsers.razor — Phase 6.1

   Staff-facing user-management page at route `/Admin/Users`. Reached from
   the sidebar's "Admin → Manage Users" link (already wired in
   MainLayout.razor, role-gated to Admin/Manager/Employee). The page is also
   independently gated by [Authorize(Roles=...)] as defense-in-depth.

   PURPOSE:
     This page is the admin/manager/employee's view of every user in the
     system (staff and customers). It exists so they can:
       1. See ALL users in a compact, paginated table.
       2. Filter by Worker ID, Full Name (text filter), Gender, Group,
          and Status (dropdown filters with colored tags).
       3. Activate or Deactivate a user (soft-delete / restore).
       4. Reset a user's password (Admin only).
       5. View a user's detail page (where group changes, role edits,
          and other per-user actions live — see UserDetail.razor).

   GROUP CHANGES:
     The inline "Change group" editor that previously lived in this table
     was removed — group changes now happen on the UserDetail page
     (/Admin/Users/{Id}) where the full role-scope rules can be applied
     with the CreateUser-style Existing/New group button UI. This page
     is read-only with respect to groups: it shows the current group
     badge and lets the viewer navigate to the detail page to change it.

   FILTERING (ERP pattern):
     All filtering is client-side via Radzen's built-in filter row
     (AllowFiltering=true, FilterMode=SimpleWithMenu). Each column has
     its own filter input in a dedicated filter row beneath the header:
       - Worker ID  → text filter (Radzen default)
       - Full Name  → text filter (Radzen default)
       - Gender     → dropdown with colored tags (Male=blue, Female=pink)
       - Group      → dropdown of available groups (no colored tags)
       - Status     → dropdown with colored tags (Active=green, Inactive=red)
     The grid loads ALL users once (PageSize=500 in the backend query)
     and Radzen handles filtering + paging client-side. Same approach
     as the ERP project's SalesList page.

   ACTIVATE / DEACTIVATE FLOW:
     - A single toggle button per row. When the user is Active, the button
       shows "Deactivate" (Danger, block icon). When Inactive, it shows
       "Activate" (Success, check_circle icon).
     - Self-deactivation is blocked client-side (button hidden on the
       current user's own row) AND server-side (handler rejects it).
     - MANAGER SCOPE (Phase 6.3, updated 6.4): A Manager (non-Admin) can
       activate/deactivate users in the Employee OR Customer role. The
       activate/deactivate button is HIDDEN on rows for other managers,
       admins, and read-onlys. A small "lock" icon with a tooltip replaces
       the button on those rows so the manager understands why it's missing.
       Admins see the button on every row except their own.

   RESET PASSWORD FLOW:
     - Admin-only (button hidden from Managers). Also hidden on the
       current user's own row (confusing UX).
     - On click: prompt via JS prompt() for new password.

   LOCALIZATION:
     All user-visible strings go through IStringLocalizer<AdminUsers>
     (Loc). Keys in AdminUsers.en-US.resx + AdminUsers.fa-IR.resx.

   ANTIFORGERY:
     Not needed — no EditForm. All actions use Wolverine command dispatch
     over the Blazor circuit. *@

@page "/Admin/Users"
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Manager,Employee")]
@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Authorization
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Authorization
@using TakOne.Application.Users.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.ActivateUser
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.DeactivateUser
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.ResetUserPassword
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Queries.GetUsersPaginated
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<AdminUsers> Loc
@inject AuthenticationStateProvider AuthStateProvider
@inject ToastService Toast
@inject IJSRuntime JS

<PageTitle>@Loc["PageTitle"]</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            .admin-header {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: space-between;
                gap: 1rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

            .worker-id-cell {
                font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", "Courier New", monospace;
                font-weight: 600;
                font-size: 0.875rem;
            }

            .user-name-cell {
                font-weight: 500;
            }

            .group-cell-none {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-style: italic;
            }

            .row-actions {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.25rem;
                justify-content: flex-end;
                align-items: center;
            }

            /* Restricted-action indicator — shown in place of the activate/
                           deactivate button when the current user is a Manager and the
                           row's user is NOT in the Employee or Customer role. Mirrors the
                           size of the text buttons it replaces so the Actions column
                           doesn't jump around when scrolling between rows. */
            .row-action-locked {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                width: 32px;
                height: 32px;
                color: var(--rz-text-tertiary-color, #9ca3af);
                cursor: help;
            }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Page header ── *@
    <div class="admin-header">
        <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
            <RadzenIcon Icon="group" Style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--rz-primary);" />
            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["PageHeading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
        </RadzenStack>

        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["CreateUserButton"]"
                      Icon="person_add"
                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                      Variant="Variant.Filled"
                      Visible="@(_isAdmin || _isManagerOnly)"
                      Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Users/Create", forceLoad: false))" />
    </div>

    @* ── Loading spinner ── *@
    @if (_isLoading)
    {
        <RadzenStack AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" JustifyContent="JustifyContent.Center"
                     Style="height: 40vh;" Gap="1rem">
            <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false"
                                       Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate"
                                       Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Large" />
            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["LoadingText"]"
                        TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);" />
        </RadzenStack>
    }

    @* ── Error banner ── *@
    else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_loadError))
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_loadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true">
            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RetryButton"]"
                          Icon="refresh"
                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                          Click="@LoadUsersAsync"
                          Style="margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
        </RadzenAlert>
    }

    @* ── User table ──
       Radzen built-in filter row (AllowFiltering + FilterMode.SimpleWithMenu).
       Worker ID and Full Name use Radzen's default text filter. Gender,
       Group, and Status use custom FilterTemplate dropdowns with colored
       badge tags. Paging is built-in (AllowPaging, PageSize=20). Data is
       loaded all at once (PageSize=500 in the backend query) and filtered
       client-side — same approach as the ERP SalesList page. *@
    else
    {
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Class="admin-users-grid" Style="padding: 0.5rem;">
            <RadzenDataGrid @ref="grid"
                            Data="@_users"
                            TItem="UserListItemDto"
                            AllowSorting="true"
                            AllowFiltering="true"
                            FilterMode="FilterMode.SimpleWithMenu"
                            FilterCaseSensitivity="FilterCaseSensitivity.CaseInsensitive"
                            AllowPaging="true"
                            PageSize="20"
                            PagerHorizontalAlign="HorizontalAlign.Center"
                            EmptyText="@Loc["EmptyText"]"
                            Style="width: 100%;"
                            RowRender="@OnRowRender">
                <Columns>

                    @* ── Worker ID — text filter (Radzen default) ── *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Property="WorkerId"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColWorkerId"]"
                                          Width="160px">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            <span class="worker-id-cell">@user.WorkerId</span>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Full Name — text filter (Radzen default) ── *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Property="FullName"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColFullName"]"
                                          Width="*">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            <span class="user-name-cell">@user.FullName</span>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Gender — dropdown filter with colored tags ──
                       Male=blue badge, Female=pink badge. The dropdown's
                       ValueTemplate shows the selected value as a colored
                       badge; Template shows each option as a colored badge.
                       AllowClear resets to null (All genders). The filter
                       is client-side via column.FilterValue. *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Property="Gender"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColGender"]"
                                          Width="140px"
                                          TextAlign="TextAlign.Center"
                                          FilterOperator="FilterOperator.Equals">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            <RadzenBadge Text="@GetGenderLabel(user.Gender)"
                                         BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Light"
                                         Style="@GetGenderBadgeStyle(user.Gender)"
                                         IsPill="true" />
                        </Template>
                        <FilterTemplate Context="column">
                            <RadzenDropDown @bind-Value="@_selectedGenderFilter"
                                            Data="@_genderFilterOptions"
                                            TValue="string"
                                            TextProperty="Label"
                                            ValueProperty="Key"
                                            AllowClear="true"
                                            Placeholder="@Loc["GenderAll"]"
                                            Change="@(args => OnGenderFilterChanged(_selectedGenderFilter, column))"
                                            Style="width: 100%; min-width: 110px;">
                                <ValueTemplate Context="selected">
                                    @{
                                        var selectedStr = selected?.ToString();
                                    }
                                    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(selectedStr))
                                    {
                                        <RadzenBadge Text="@GetGenderLabel(selectedStr)"
                                                     BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Light"
                                                     Style="@GetGenderBadgeStyle(selectedStr)"
                                                     IsPill="true" />
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <span>@Loc["GenderAll"]</span>
                                    }
                                </ValueTemplate>
                                <Template Context="option">
                                    @{
                                        var item = (GenderFilterOption)option;
                                    }
                                    <RadzenBadge Text="@item.Label"
                                                 BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Light"
                                                 Style="@GetGenderBadgeStyle(item.Key)"
                                                 IsPill="true" />
                                </Template>
                            </RadzenDropDown>
                        </FilterTemplate>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Group — dropdown filter, no colored tags ──
                       Plain dropdown listing all available groups (derived
                       from the loaded users). AllowClear resets to null
                       (All groups). Filter is client-side via
                       column.FilterValue. *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Property="GroupName"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColGroup"]"
                                          Width="180px"
                                          FilterOperator="FilterOperator.Equals">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            @if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(user.GroupName))
                            {
                                <span class="group-cell-none">@Loc["GroupNone"]</span>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <RadzenBadge Text="@user.GroupName"
                                             BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Base"
                                             IsPill="true" />
                            }
                        </Template>
                        <FilterTemplate Context="column">
                            <RadzenDropDown @bind-Value="@_selectedGroupFilter"
                                            Data="@_availableGroups"
                                            TValue="string"
                                            AllowClear="true"
                                            Placeholder="@Loc["GroupAll"]"
                                            Change="@(args => OnGroupFilterChanged(_selectedGroupFilter, column))"
                                            Style="width: 100%; min-width: 130px;" />
                        </FilterTemplate>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Status — dropdown filter with colored tags ──
                       Active=green badge, Inactive=red badge. The dropdown
                       uses string keys ("Active"/"Inactive") which are
                       mapped to booleans for the IsActive column filter.
                       AllowClear resets to null (All statuses). *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Property="IsActive"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColStatus"]"
                                          Width="140px"
                                          TextAlign="TextAlign.Center"
                                          FilterOperator="FilterOperator.Equals">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            <RadzenBadge Text="@GetStatusLabel(user.IsActive)"
                                         BadgeStyle="@GetStatusBadgeStyle(user.IsActive)"
                                         IsPill="true" />
                        </Template>
                        <FilterTemplate Context="column">
                            <RadzenDropDown @bind-Value="@_selectedStatusFilter"
                                            Data="@_statusFilterOptions"
                                            TValue="string"
                                            AllowClear="true"
                                            Placeholder="@Loc["StatusAll"]"
                                            Change="@(args => OnStatusFilterChanged(_selectedStatusFilter, column))"
                                            Style="width: 100%; min-width: 130px;">
                                <ValueTemplate Context="selected">
                                    @{
                                        var selectedStr = selected?.ToString();
                                    }
                                    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(selectedStr))
                                    {
                                        <RadzenBadge Text="@GetStatusLabel(selectedStr)"
                                                     BadgeStyle="@GetStatusBadgeStyle(selectedStr)"
                                                     IsPill="true" />
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <span>@Loc["StatusAll"]</span>
                                    }
                                </ValueTemplate>
                                <Template Context="statusOption">
                                    <RadzenBadge Text="@GetStatusLabel(statusOption)"
                                                 BadgeStyle="@GetStatusBadgeStyle(statusOption)"
                                                 IsPill="true" />
                                </Template>
                            </RadzenDropDown>
                        </FilterTemplate>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Actions ── *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColActions"]"
                                          Width="220px"
                                          TextAlign="TextAlign.Center"
                                          Sortable="false"
                                          Filterable="false">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            <div class="row-actions">
                                @* View details — navigates to user detail page.
                                   All viewers (Admin/Manager/Employee) can navigate;
                                   the detail page enforces its own per-action gates. *@
                                <RadzenButton Icon="visibility"
                                              Variant="Variant.Text"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Info"
                                              title="@Loc["ActionViewDetail"]"
                                              aria-label="@Loc["ActionViewDetail"]"
                                              Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo($"/Admin/Users/{user.Id}", forceLoad: false))" />

                                @* Activate / Deactivate toggle.
                                   Hidden on the current user's own row —
                                   self-deactivation is rejected by the
                                   handler anyway, but the button adds
                                   confusing UX so we just don't show it.
                                   When the user is Active → show Deactivate
                                   (Danger, block icon). When Inactive → show
                                   Activate (Success, check_circle icon).

                                   MANAGER SCOPE (Phase 6.3, updated 6.4):
                                   If the current user is a Manager (not
                                   Admin), the button is only shown on rows
                                   whose user is in the Employee OR Customer
                                   role. On other rows (managers, admins,
                                   read-onlys), a small "lock" icon with a
                                   tooltip replaces the button so the manager
                                   understands why it's missing. Admins see
                                   the button on every row except their own.

                                   EMPLOYEE VIEWERS (Phase 6.5):
                                   Employees can't activate/deactivate anyone —
                                   the button is hidden on every row AND no
                                   lock icon is shown (the lock is a Manager-only
                                   affordance; for Employees the entire
                                   activate/deactivate feature is off-limits,
                                   so showing locks everywhere would be noisy). *@
                                @if (user.Id != _currentUserId && (_isAdmin || _isManagerOnly))
                                {
                                    @if (CanActOn(user))
                                    {
                                        @if (user.IsActive)
                                        {
                                            <RadzenButton Icon="block"
                                                          Variant="Variant.Text"
                                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                                          title="@Loc["ActionDeactivate"]"
                                                          aria-label="@Loc["ActionDeactivate"]"
                                                          Disabled="@(_isBusyUserId == user.Id)"
                                                          Click="@(() => HandleDeactivateAsync(user))" />
                                        }
                                        else
                                        {
                                            <RadzenButton Icon="check_circle"
                                                          Variant="Variant.Text"
                                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Success"
                                                          title="@Loc["ActionActivate"]"
                                                          aria-label="@Loc["ActionActivate"]"
                                                          Disabled="@(_isBusyUserId == user.Id)"
                                                          Click="@(() => HandleActivateAsync(user))" />
                                        }
                                    }
                                    else if (_isManagerOnly)
                                    {
                                        @* Manager can't act on this row — show a lock icon
                                           with a tooltip explaining why. aria-label gives
                                           screen readers the same explanation. Only shown
                                           for Managers (not Employees) since Employees
                                           can't activate/deactivate anyone — locks would
                                           be noisy. *@
                                        <span class="row-action-locked"
                                              title="@Loc["ActionLockedForManager"]"
                                              aria-label="@Loc["ActionLockedForManager"]">
                                            <RadzenIcon Icon="lock" Style="font-size: 1.1rem;" />
                                        </span>
                                    }
                                }

                                @* Reset password — Admin only. *@
                                @if (_isAdmin && user.Id != _currentUserId)
                                {
                                    <RadzenButton Icon="vpn_key"
                                                  Variant="Variant.Text"
                                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Warning"
                                                  title="@Loc["ActionResetPassword"]"
                                                  aria-label="@Loc["ActionResetPassword"]"
                                                  Disabled="@(_isBusyUserId == user.Id)"
                                                  Click="@(() => HandleResetPasswordAsync(user))" />
                                }
                            </div>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>
                </Columns>
            </RadzenDataGrid>
        </RadzenCard>
    }
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── State ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private List<UserListItemDto> _users = new();
    private List<string> _availableGroups = new();

    private RadzenDataGrid<UserListItemDto> grid = default!;

    // Filter state — each nullable; null = "no filter" (AllowClear=true
    // on the RadzenDropDown passes null when the user clears).
    // Status and Gender use string keys that are mapped to the actual
    // property type in the filter handler. Group uses the group name
    // string directly.
    private string? _selectedStatusFilter;
    private string? _selectedGenderFilter;
    private string? _selectedGroupFilter;

    // Status filter options — string keys "Active"/"Inactive" (culture-
    // neutral). The display text comes from GetStatusLabel(string) which
    // maps to localized resx values.
    private readonly List<string> _statusFilterOptions = new()
    {
        "Active", "Inactive"
    };

    // Gender filter options — Key is "Male"/"Female" (culture-neutral),
    // Label is the localized display text.
    private List<GenderFilterOption> _genderFilterOptions = new();

    private sealed class GenderFilterOption
    {
        public string Key { get; init; } = string.Empty;
        public string Label { get; init; } = string.Empty;
    }

    private bool _isLoading = true;
    private string _loadError = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// The Id of the user whose action button is currently in flight.
    /// Null when no action is pending. Used to disable that row's action
    /// buttons while the round-trip is in progress (prevents double-clicks).
    /// </summary>
    private Guid? _isBusyUserId;

    /// <summary>
    /// The current user's Id — used to hide self-action buttons
    /// (self-deactivation, self-password-reset) on the user's own row.
    /// </summary>
    private Guid _currentUserId;

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether the current user is in the Admin role. Computed via
    /// AuthenticationStateProvider in OnInitializedAsync — NOT via
    /// ICurrentUserService.IsInRole (which returns false for everyone in
    /// interactive Blazor Server mode because HttpContext is null over
    /// the SignalR circuit).
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isAdmin;

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether the current user is in the Manager role (and NOT also in
    /// the Admin role). Used to gate the activate/deactivate button:
    /// a Manager can only act on users in the Employee OR Customer role —
    /// other managers, admins, and read-onlys are off-limits. Admins (who
    /// may also be in the Manager role) bypass this restriction, so we
    /// explicitly check `!_isAdmin` here.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isManagerOnly;

    // ── Lifecycle ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // Populate the gender-filter dropdown options from localizer.
        _genderFilterOptions = new List<GenderFilterOption>
        {
            new() { Key = "Male",   Label = Loc["GenderMale"] },
            new() { Key = "Female", Label = Loc["GenderFemale"] }
        };

        // Resolve the current user's Id + Admin/Manager roles via the Blazor auth
        // state (NOT ICurrentUserService — see field doc on _isAdmin).
        try
        {
            var authState = await AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync();
            var user = authState.User;

            if (user?.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true)
            {
                var idClaim = user.FindFirst("UserId")?.Value
                              ?? user.FindFirst(System.Security.Claims.ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier)?.Value;
                if (Guid.TryParse(idClaim, out var parsedId))
                {
                    _currentUserId = parsedId;
                }

                _isAdmin = user.IsInRole(Roles.Admin);
                // Manager-only means "in Manager role AND not also Admin".
                // Admins who happen to also be in the Manager role are
                // treated as Admins (no restriction).
                _isManagerOnly = !_isAdmin && user.IsInRole(Roles.Manager);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            // Non-fatal — _currentUserId stays Guid.Empty (no self-action
            // buttons hidden, which is safe but slightly worse UX) and
            // _isAdmin stays false (Reset Password button hidden — safer
            // fallback if role resolution fails). _isManagerOnly also
            // stays false (no Manager restriction applied — admins always
            // pass through, which is the safer fallback).
        }

        await LoadUsersAsync();
    }

    // ── Data loading ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadUsersAsync()
    {
        _isLoading = true;
        _loadError = string.Empty;

        try
        {
            // Load all users — filtering and paging are client-side via
            // Radzen's built-in filter row + pager (same approach as the
            // ERP SalesList page). PageSize=500 ensures we get everything
            // in one round-trip.
            var query = new GetUsersPaginatedQuery
            {
                PageNumber = 1,
                PageSize = 500
            };

            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<PaginatedResult<UserListItemDto>>(query);

            _users = result.Items.ToList();

            // Derive the available groups from the loaded users for the
            // group filter dropdown. Only non-empty, distinct group names.
            _availableGroups = _users
                .Select(u => u.GroupName)
                .Where(g => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(g))
                .Select(g => g!)
                .Distinct()
                .OrderBy(g => g)
                .ToList();
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            _loadError = Loc["Error_FailedToLoad"];
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Filter handlers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Each handler sets column.FilterValue and calls grid.Reload() to
    // trigger Radzen's client-side filtering. The bound field is updated
    // by @bind-Value before the Change event fires, so we pass the field
    // (not the args parameter) to the handler.

    private async Task OnStatusFilterChanged(string? value, RadzenDataGridColumn<UserListItemDto> column)
    {
        _selectedStatusFilter = value;

        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(value))
        {
            column.FilterValue = null;
        }
        else
        {
            // Map the string key to a boolean for the IsActive column.
            column.FilterValue = value == "Active";
            column.FilterOperator = FilterOperator.Equals;
        }

        await grid.Reload();
    }

    private async Task OnGenderFilterChanged(string? value, RadzenDataGridColumn<UserListItemDto> column)
    {
        _selectedGenderFilter = value;

        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(value))
        {
            column.FilterValue = null;
        }
        else
        {
            // Map the string key to the Gender enum for the Gender column.
            column.FilterValue = value == "Male"
                ? Domain.Users.Gender.Male
                : Domain.Users.Gender.Female;
            column.FilterOperator = FilterOperator.Equals;
        }

        await grid.Reload();
    }

    private async Task OnGroupFilterChanged(string? value, RadzenDataGridColumn<UserListItemDto> column)
    {
        _selectedGroupFilter = value;

        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(value))
        {
            column.FilterValue = null;
        }
        else
        {
            column.FilterValue = value;
            column.FilterOperator = FilterOperator.Equals;
        }

        await grid.Reload();
    }

    // ── Activate / Deactivate ───────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns true if the current user may activate/deactivate the given
    /// row's user.
    ///
    /// Rules:
    ///   - Admins  → may act on anyone (except themselves, which is checked
    ///               separately in the markup).
    ///   - Managers → may only act on users whose <c>Roles</c> collection
    ///                contains <c>Roles.Employee</c> OR <c>Roles.Customer</c>.
    ///                This excludes other managers, admins, and read-onlys.
    ///   - Employees → cannot activate/deactivate anyone (the feature is
    ///                Admin/Manager only). Returns false for all rows.
    ///
    /// The server-side handlers (ActivateUserCommandHandler /
    /// DeactivateUserCommandHandler) enforce the same rule as
    /// defense-in-depth against tampered requests.
    /// </summary>
    private bool CanActOn(UserListItemDto user)
    {
        // Admins can act on anyone (the markup already hides the button on
        // the admin's own row — we don't re-check that here).
        if (_isAdmin) return true;

        // Managers (non-Admin) can act on Employees OR Customers.
        if (_isManagerOnly)
        {
            return user.Roles.Contains(Roles.Employee)
                || user.Roles.Contains(Roles.Customer);
        }

        // Employees (and anyone else) — cannot activate/deactivate anyone.
        // The markup hides the button entirely for non-Admin/Manager viewers.
        return false;
    }

    private async Task HandleDeactivateAsync(UserListItemDto user)
    {
        if (_isBusyUserId.HasValue) return;

        // JS confirm() — destructive action deserves one click of friction.
        // The handler also rejects self-deactivation as defense-in-depth,
        // but we hide the button on the user's own row anyway (see markup).
        var confirmMessage = string.Format(
            CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
            Loc["ConfirmDeactivate"],
            user.FullName,
            user.WorkerId);

        var confirmed = await JS.InvokeAsync<bool>("confirm", confirmMessage);
        if (!confirmed) return;

        _isBusyUserId = user.Id;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new DeactivateUserCommand(user.Id));

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["DeactivateSuccess"], user.FullName),
                    summary: Loc["DeactivateSuccessTitle"]);
                await LoadUsersAsync();
            }
            else
            {
                // The handler rejects self-deactivation with a friendly
                // message; surface it verbatim.
                await Toast.Error(
                    result.Error ?? Loc["ActionError"],
                    summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.Error(Loc["ActionError"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBusyUserId = null;
        }
    }

    private async Task HandleActivateAsync(UserListItemDto user)
    {
        if (_isBusyUserId.HasValue) return;

        // No confirmation for activation — it's a non-destructive restore.
        _isBusyUserId = user.Id;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new ActivateUserCommand(user.Id));

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["ActivateSuccess"], user.FullName),
                    summary: Loc["ActivateSuccessTitle"]);
